{# The calendar, on its own page.

   WHY IT IS NOT ON THE MAIN PAGE. Twenty-eight rows each reading "papers
   not published yet" made half that page carry no information, and a
   phrase repeated that often teaches the eye to skip — which would hide
   the one row that mattered. Here the repetition is the point: this is a
   diary, and a diary is meant to be scanned.

   A REAL PAGE, NOT A TAB. Same build-time pattern as the register's
   filters and the roadworks views: its own URL, a plain link to reach it,
   bookmarkable, indexable, working with JavaScript switched off. LCC can
   keep this one open before a meeting.

   THE HORIZON IS THE COUNCIL'S, NOT OURS. Each committee page shows
   whatever window it chooses, so this reaches as far as they publish and
   no further. In January it will show a different set. The page says so
   rather than implying it sees the whole year. #}

<div class="wrap">
{% if not agenda.ok or not agenda.scheduledByMonth | length %}
  <p class="agenda-none">No meetings are currently listed. The council publishes
  its committee dates some months in advance, so this is unusual — it more
  likely means the calendar has not been collected recently.</p>
{% else %}

<p class="agenda-intro">These are the meetings North Ayrshire Council has in its
diary. <strong>Most will have no papers yet</strong> — they are normally
published about three days beforehand, and until then there is no way to know
whether Largs is in them. Where papers have appeared, the row says so.</p>

<p class="agenda-sub">{{ agenda.counts.scheduled }} meetings listed{% if
agenda.scheduledTo %}, up to {{ agenda.scheduledTo }}{% endif %}. That is as far
as the council has published; more will appear as they set the dates.</p>

{% for month in agenda.scheduledByMonth %}
<h2 class="agenda-month">{{ month.label }}</h2>
<ul class="agenda-list agenda-quiet">
{% for m in month.meetings %}
  <li class="agenda-row{% if m.state == 'nothing' %} agenda-checked{% endif %}">
    <p class="agenda-when">{{ m.display }}</p>
    <p class="agenda-what">
      {% if m.url %}<a href="{{ m.url }}">{{ m.committee }}</a>
      {% else %}{{ m.committee }}{% endif %}
      {%- if m.state == "nothing" %} <span class="agenda-tag">papers out · no mention of Largs</span>{% endif %}
    </p>
  </li>
{% endfor %}
</ul>
{% endfor %}

<p class="agenda-note"><a href="/on-the-agenda/">← Back to North Ayrshire Council</a></p>

{% endif %}
</div>
